---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="For schools and colleges"
	description="Wheel booking, kiln firing queues and semester courses for school and college ceramics departments with one or two kilns."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">For schools &amp; colleges</p>
			<h1>A ceramics department that runs on the timetable, not the clipboard.</h1>
			<p class="lede narrow">
				One or two kilns, a semester of courses, and students grabbing a wheel between classes.
				Kilnbook keeps the wheels, the kiln shelves and the class lists in one place, so the studio
				technician is not the only one who knows what is going on.
			</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Wheels booked between classes</h2>
		<p>
			Students reserve wheels, hand-building tables and the slab roller in one-hour blocks, so a free
			period does not start with a walk to the studio to find every wheel taken. Set
			how many hours a week each group gets and how far ahead they can book, and freed-up slots appear
			on the calendar right away. A tablet by the door shows who is in the room while the kilns are
			running. <a href="/features/wheel-time">How wheel time works</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Firings for one or two kilns</h2>
		<p>
			Students log a piece when they put it on the bisque shelf. Each kiln has its own queue for
			bisque and glaze loads, you can see how full each load is, and every firing is recorded with
			the date, cone, schedule and who loaded it. When a load comes out, students get a text, which
			means fewer pieces left on the shelf at the end of term.
			<a href="/features/firings">How firings work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Courses that follow the semester</h2>
		<p>
			Set up each course as a fixed series that runs for the length of your term, alongside any
			drop-in open studio sessions. Instructors get their own login with today's roster, can mark
			attendance from the studio tablet, and leave notes for whoever teaches the next section.
			<a href="/features/classes">How classes work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Which plan?</h2>
		<p>
			Most departments with one or two kilns fit the Studio plan, which covers up to 3 kilns with
			unlimited members, so every student on the roster can have an account. A department with a
			single kiln can start on Starter. School ceramics programs get 30% off any plan.
			<a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Questions departments ask</h2>
		<div class="faq">
			<details>
				<summary>We only have one or two kilns. Which plan do we need?</summary>
				<p>
					The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns, so two kilns fit with room for one more. If you only
					run a single kiln, the Starter plan covers it.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Is there a discount for schools and colleges?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. School ceramics programs get 30% off any plan. Mention it when you book a demo.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Can we set up a whole year group at once?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. Upload a CSV with names and emails, and we map the columns for you during setup.
				</p>
			</details>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>See it with your timetable.</h2>
			<p>We will walk through your kilns, your courses and your open studio hours on a short call.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
